### Voice AI — Phase 2: Conversational AI Receptionist (2026-06-04)
The AI now TALKS to callers instead of just forwarding. When a client's
voice_agents.ai_enabled=true, the call becomes a two-way conversation: caller
speaks → Twilio transcribes → Claude answers from the client's knowledge base →
speaks the reply → listens again, transferring to a human or ending only when it
decides to. Built on Twilio's built-in speech <Gather> (no Media-Streams
websockets, no external STT/TTS vendors) so it reuses Claude + the existing KB and
stays inside the signed-webhook model.

- voice.js — new route POST /voice/respond (handleVoiceRespond) drives one
  conversational turn; /voice/incoming branches into AI mode when ai_enabled +
  anthropic present (greeting + <Gather input="speech">). Conversation state
  (turns + cached KB + no-input count) persists on voice_calls.metadata across
  turns; transcript column accumulates the readable dialog.
- Pure, unit-tested helpers: cleanForSpeech (strip tokens/URLs/markdown/emoji for
  TTS), parseAgentDecision ([TRANSFER]/[END] control tokens), detectCallerEndIntent,
  buildReceptionistSystemPrompt (spoken-reply rules + KB), buildGatherTwiml,
  buildTranscript. Claude callers: generateVoiceReply (model claude-haiku-4-5 for
  low latency, 200 tok) + summarizeVoiceCall (post-call one-line summary + outcome
  classification, JSON out).
- handleVoiceStatus: on FINAL call completion (gated off the mid-call Dial action),
  generates summary + outcome once (idempotent).
- db1_voice.sql: + voice_agents.ai_enabled boolean default false (applied; demo
  agent flipped true with an AI greeting). Phase 1 forward/voicemail stays the
  default for any agent with ai_enabled=false.
- Tests: testVoiceAI() extended (+~15 assertions) — cleanForSpeech, decision
  parsing, end-intent, system prompt, Gather TwiML, transcript, /voice/respond
  graceful reprompt. Verified end-to-end by booting the server.
- Next: Phase 3 (lead qualification + missed-call SMS recovery), Phase 4 (shared
  spam network), Phase 5 (industry agents). Optional: Media Streams speech-to-speech
  latency upgrade behind the same routes.

